      "id": "P-23a45e2f19",
      "title": "Burgers \u00b7 inspectable research attempt",
      "canonical_statement": "Worked example authored for this studio, not an imported research paper.\nConsider the inviscid Burgers equation u_t + u*u_x = 0.\nAssume a smooth classical solution while following a characteristic dx/dt = u.\nSet m = u_x along that characteristic. Differentiating the PDE yields dm/dt = -m**2.\nFor m(0) = -1, the reduced equation gives m(t) = -1/(1-t) while t < 1.\nThis reduced calculation does not solve the Navier-Stokes global regularity problem.\nOpen question: which assumptions allow a related mechanism in a different PDE?",
